WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:03.000
&gt;&gt;&gt; This morning the Ukrainian

00:00:03.107 --> 00:00:04.275
military says Russia launched

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.672
more than 50 cruise missiles in

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:07.083
yet another wave of strikes

00:00:07.216 --> 00:00:08.250
targeting critical

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.201
infrastructure in Kyiv and

00:00:09.365 --> 00:00:10.664
cities across the country.

00:00:10.806 --> 00:00:12.207
Ukraine claiming it intercepted

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.581
44 of those missiles.

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:15.480
Kyiv's mayor, though, says one

00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:16.756
attack hit an energy facility

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:18.686
that powered some 350,000

00:00:18.782 --> 00:00:19.216
apartments.

00:00:19.329 --> 00:00:21.397
CNN's nic Robertson joining us

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:22.019
live from Kyiv.

00:00:22.466 --> 00:00:23.701
As I understand it you are in an

00:00:23.881 --> 00:00:25.516
area where one of the lines

00:00:25.982 --> 00:00:27.450
there -- you are at a line where

00:00:27.536 --> 00:00:29.304
people are trying to get water,

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.865
the mayor has also said some 80%

00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:32.883
of the city's population doesn't

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.923
have water supply right now

00:00:34.097 --> 00:00:35.800
because of the attacks.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.801
What more can you tell us about

00:00:37.975 --> 00:00:40.037
just how significant that damage

00:00:40.154 --> 00:00:40.621
is?

00:00:42.134 --> 00:00:43.068
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Yeah, the mayor

00:00:43.201 --> 00:00:44.135
says he hopes to get the

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:45.336
supplies up and running, part of

00:00:46.471 --> 00:00:47.705
the city the water is coming

00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:49.573
back on, but here you have a

00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:52.108
line of people, this water

00:00:52.175 --> 00:00:53.009
spigot they are lining up for

00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:55.711
here is one of dozens around the

00:00:56.112 --> 00:00:57.112
city.
So this is how people are going

00:00:57.112 --> 00:01:00.115
to be getting their water in the

00:01:00.115 --> 00:01:02.116
coming days until the city

00:01:02.216 --> 00:01:04.251
officials can get the water

00:01:04.385 --> 00:01:06.586
supplies back up and running.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.721
People I have been talking to

00:01:08.121 --> 00:01:09.589
here tell me they are okay with

00:01:09.722 --> 00:01:10.923
this, obviously they don't like

00:01:11.557 --> 00:01:13.025
T but they're okay with it, it's

00:01:13.158 --> 00:01:14.259
not going to make them leave the

00:01:14.393 --> 00:01:14.793
city.

00:01:14.793 --> 00:01:16.628
They're going to stay here.

00:01:16.761 --> 00:01:18.396
They expected the situation to

00:01:18.529 --> 00:01:19.030
get worse.

00:01:19.096 --> 00:01:20.397
Russia has been hitting the

00:01:20.531 --> 00:01:22.332
power generating facilities

00:01:22.466 --> 00:01:24.167
across this country now for

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.468
about three weeks and it's

00:01:25.602 --> 00:01:28.704
reduced the capacity of the

00:01:28.837 --> 00:01:31.239
power grid to really keep a lot

00:01:31.373 --> 00:01:32.841
of the main functions in big

00:01:32.974 --> 00:01:36.377
cities like Kyiv up and running.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.812
That meeting today with strikes

00:01:38.945 --> 00:01:39.679
today they have been able to

00:01:39.813 --> 00:01:41.814
take out so much of the water

00:01:42.148 --> 00:01:42.648
capacity in the city.

00:01:42.648 --> 00:01:45.617
Also across the city the

00:01:45.751 --> 00:01:47.619
cellular network normally a good

00:01:47.752 --> 00:01:51.255
4G signal now reduced to a poor

00:01:51.389 --> 00:01:52.156
3G signal.

00:01:52.156 --> 00:01:54.324
The impacts are beginning to be

00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:55.525
felt more widely.

00:01:55.659 --> 00:01:56.493
The government saying today ten

00:01:56.626 --> 00:01:57.160
different regions were affected

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.329
by strikes, 18 different

00:02:00.462 --> 00:02:02.531
strikes, a hydropower plant

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:04.899
north of Kyiv was impacted today

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.234
as well as the biggest hydro

00:02:07.368 --> 00:02:08.169
electric power plant in the

00:02:08.269 --> 00:02:10.170
center of Ukraine that was also

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.639
hit.
The key part of Russia's efforts

00:02:12.772 --> 00:02:17.609
here is to just -- is to stop

00:02:17.743 --> 00:02:18.877
the electrical generating

00:02:18.977 --> 00:02:20.912
facilities in the country, stop

00:02:21.045 --> 00:02:23.781
the grid working.

00:02:24.181 --> 00:02:25.616
&gt;&gt; It is something especially

00:02:25.616 --> 00:02:26.183
when you see those pictures and

00:02:26.216 --> 00:02:27.517
those numbers, people lining up

00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:29.485
for that water and their

00:02:29.619 --> 00:02:30.119
resolve.

00:02:30.186 --> 00:02:30.987
Appreciate it.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.521
Thank you.

00:02:32.521 --> 00:02:33.122
&gt;&gt;&gt; Joining me to discuss

00:02:33.255 --> 00:02:37.659
further Andrea Kendall Taylor.

00:02:37.792 --> 00:02:38.826
Good to see you this morning.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.161
When we look at what happened

00:02:41.295 --> 00:02:43.863
today, when we look at this

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.498
pressure that Russia and

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:47.199
Vladimir Putin are trying to put

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.568
on Ukrainians by specifically

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:50.435
targeting infrastructure, not

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:53.371
just electricity, but water,

00:02:53.504 --> 00:02:55.272
what does this tell you about

00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:57.474
Putin's plan moving forward?

00:02:57.608 --> 00:03:00.210
Could he be moving further west

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.511
ultimately to target some of

00:03:01.644 --> 00:03:02.245
those infrastructure -- some of

00:03:02.378 --> 00:03:04.246
the infrastructure there as

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:04.880
well?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.248
&gt;&gt; Well, I think, I mean, as

00:03:06.248 --> 00:03:07.849
you're covering the attacks are

00:03:08.249 --> 00:03:09.450
horrific and we should not grow

00:03:09.584 --> 00:03:11.385
to -- grow immune to them, but

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:13.053
they shouldn't be surprising,

00:03:13.187 --> 00:03:14.488
and I think the way that we

00:03:14.621 --> 00:03:17.757
understand these attacks is that

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:19.325
as Vladimir Putin is unable to

00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:21.460
accomplish his objectives on the

00:03:21.593 --> 00:03:23.561
battlefield, he will continue to

00:03:23.695 --> 00:03:24.829
terrorize Ukrainian cities, he

00:03:24.963 --> 00:03:26.464
will continue to terrorize

00:03:26.597 --> 00:03:27.298
Ukrainians to try to get them to

00:03:27.298 --> 00:03:30.300
make concessions and end the war

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.234
on Russia's terms.

00:03:31.368 --> 00:03:34.737
But you covered an interesting

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:35.571
point, Erica, you noted that

00:03:35.704 --> 00:03:38.707
Ukraine shot down 44 out of the

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.774
50 missiles that Russia launched

00:03:39.908 --> 00:03:42.276
and it just underscores how

00:03:42.276 --> 00:03:43.777
critical the air defenses are

00:03:43.911 --> 00:03:45.646
that the west continues to

00:03:45.779 --> 00:03:47.747
provide Ukraine and that will be

00:03:47.881 --> 00:03:49.515
key to preventing Putin from

00:03:49.649 --> 00:03:51.717
moving west with those attacks.

00:03:51.851 --> 00:03:53.452
&gt;&gt; There's not just the

00:03:53.585 --> 00:03:54.286
infrastructure that we're

00:03:54.353 --> 00:03:56.488
following, right, as those

00:03:56.621 --> 00:03:57.655
attacks continue, but also the

00:03:57.789 --> 00:03:59.056
fact that Russia is now pulling

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.457
out of this grain deal.

00:04:00.591 --> 00:04:01.725
Earlier today the Kremlin called

00:04:01.858 --> 00:04:05.261
T quote, risky and dangerous.

00:04:05.395 --> 00:04:06.462
What do you see as the path

00:04:06.596 --> 00:04:07.396
forward here?

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.330
Is this just another way that,

00:04:08.464 --> 00:04:11.433
you know, that Putin is

00:04:11.566 --> 00:04:13.701
essentially trying to hold

00:04:13.835 --> 00:04:14.335
Ukraine hostage?

00:04:14.435 --> 00:04:15.803
And potentially Europe?

00:04:15.936 --> 00:04:16.537
&gt;&gt; Exactly.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.838
I think -- yeah, exactly.

00:04:17.971 --> 00:04:19.839
Both of these represent forms of

00:04:19.873 --> 00:04:20.373
escalation.

00:04:20.373 --> 00:04:21.307
So, again, as he can't

00:04:21.441 --> 00:04:24.310
accomplish on the battlefield,

00:04:24.443 --> 00:04:26.311
he's looking for any options,

00:04:26.311 --> 00:04:27.112
he's leveraging any remaining

00:04:27.245 --> 00:04:31.949
influence -- or, I'm sorry, he's

00:04:32.316 --> 00:04:32.816
weaponizing any remaining

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:33.950
leverage that he has.

00:04:34.317 --> 00:04:35.719
And I think that attacks on the

00:04:35.852 --> 00:04:37.453
civilian centers and his

00:04:37.587 --> 00:04:40.956
suspension of the grain deal are

00:04:41.056 --> 00:04:41.557
related.

00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:43.425
As the lights go out and it gets

00:04:43.558 --> 00:04:45.426
colder, we're likely to see an

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.361
influx of Ukrainian migrants

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:48.329
into Europe.

00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:50.363
I also think that Putin is

00:04:50.363 --> 00:04:51.965
calculating with an increase in

00:04:52.365 --> 00:04:54.700
prices, more food insecurity,

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.001
potentially instability in the

00:04:56.335 --> 00:04:57.402
south and the Middle East, that

00:04:57.536 --> 00:04:59.137
that, too, could push another

00:04:59.271 --> 00:05:01.105
wave of migrants up into Europe

00:05:01.239 --> 00:05:02.340
to the south.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.341
So those two things could very

00:05:04.341 --> 00:05:05.776
well converged and put

00:05:05.909 --> 00:05:07.610
tremendous pressure on European

00:05:07.744 --> 00:05:08.344
governments.

00:05:08.411 --> 00:05:09.512
So I think it's Europe that he

00:05:09.645 --> 00:05:11.480
has in his cross hairs and he's

00:05:11.614 --> 00:05:14.783
trying to make their support for

00:05:14.916 --> 00:05:16.951
Ukraine as costly as possible to

00:05:17.085 --> 00:05:19.753
get them to stop their support

00:05:19.887 --> 00:05:21.655
because this is a critical

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:22.456
juncture for Putin.

00:05:22.589 --> 00:05:25.158
He needs to make it through this

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.559
winter without losing additional

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:27.359
territory so he is weaponizing

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.194
everything he's got.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.362
&gt;&gt; There's so much talk about

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:31.396
how difficult this winter is

00:05:31.529 --> 00:05:33.231
going to be in Ukraine, for

00:05:33.364 --> 00:05:34.398
obvious reasons we just

00:05:34.465 --> 00:05:35.533
discussed, also in Europe as we

00:05:35.666 --> 00:05:37.234
know, we see the prices, we know

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.368
what's happening there, we know

00:05:38.502 --> 00:05:39.469
what the stressors are at that

00:05:39.602 --> 00:05:41.270
point, but the reality is there

00:05:41.404 --> 00:05:42.371
has been reporting from the

00:05:42.371 --> 00:05:43.639
beginning of the war about how

00:05:43.739 --> 00:05:45.841
low morale was among Russian

00:05:46.007 --> 00:05:47.342
troops, now all of this added

00:05:47.475 --> 00:05:48.743
reporting about how ill prepared

00:05:48.876 --> 00:05:49.377
they are.

00:05:49.377 --> 00:05:51.712
The impact of this upcoming

00:05:51.845 --> 00:05:54.848
winter, I mean, that could also

00:05:54.981 --> 00:05:57.383
lead to even further dis consent

00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:58.517
among these troops, these

00:05:58.651 --> 00:06:00.552
Russian troops.

00:06:00.686 --> 00:06:03.088
&gt;&gt; I entirely agree and I think

00:06:03.221 --> 00:06:03.955
the key flash point is going to

00:06:04.088 --> 00:06:06.691
be the battle over kherson.

00:06:06.824 --> 00:06:08.092
We know that Ukraine continues

00:06:08.425 --> 00:06:09.993
to make progress there and a lot

00:06:10.427 --> 00:06:11.227
of those Russian fighters have

00:06:11.361 --> 00:06:13.162
been there for a very long time

00:06:13.296 --> 00:06:15.464
and we know that their supply

00:06:15.598 --> 00:06:17.266
lines have been significantly

00:06:17.399 --> 00:06:18.767
disrupted.

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:19.367
So it's going to make it very

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.469
hard for Moscow to get winter

00:06:21.602 --> 00:06:23.370
gear into the soldiers there.

00:06:23.504 --> 00:06:26.439
So that low morale, I think,

00:06:26.439 --> 00:06:27.674
make it increasingly likely that

00:06:27.807 --> 00:06:29.675
Ukraine will have success in the

00:06:29.809 --> 00:06:30.643
coming weeks or a couple of

00:06:30.776 --> 00:06:33.045
months in that area.

00:06:33.178 --> 00:06:34.446
But the one thing to note is I

00:06:34.446 --> 00:06:37.482
think there's a lot of optimism

00:06:37.615 --> 00:06:38.749
in the west about how well

00:06:39.617 --> 00:06:40.851
Ukraine is doing, but even with

00:06:40.984 --> 00:06:43.286
low morale I think it's still

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.454
unlikely that Russian forces

00:06:44.454 --> 00:06:46.455
will entirely collapse.

